# Remora's guest (bd remora-7oih.5). Alpine's own, less the gettys (there is no console to log in
# on, and no password to log in with), with sshd, dockerd and acpid run by init itself.
#
# Why init: Android writes to /proc/sysrq-trigger when its shutdown cannot unmount /data — which
# a fresh profile's first boot always reaches, since it reboots itself once — and that trigger is
# the KERNEL's, not the container's. "Terminate all tasks" took sshd and docker down with it and
# left a guest nobody could reach (seen). Writes to the trigger bypass kernel.sysrq, so
# no sysctl stops them; init is the one process they spare, and it respawns these at once. An
# OpenRC-driven restart was tried first and stalled on OpenRC's own state after the kill.
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc sysinit
::sysinit:/sbin/openrc boot
::wait:/sbin/openrc default
::respawn:/usr/sbin/remora-run sshd
::respawn:/usr/sbin/remora-run dockerd
::respawn:/usr/sbin/remora-run acpid
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/sbin/openrc shutdown
